.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/agent-memory-local/

# Evidence exceptions (2026-08-18): committed flight/gate artifacts — small JSON/PNG evidence only,
# never raw frame dumps. The 2026-08-05 live-demo log was lost to a clobber + gitignore; committed
# evidence is how that never repeats (CI validates *flight_log*.json via check_live_flight_log.py).
# NOTE the level-by-level pattern: a DIRECTORY exclude (dir/) cannot be pierced by child negations,
# so each level excludes CONTENTS (dir/*) and re-includes the evidence children.
!eval/results/live_flight_log_*.json
# ...and the acknowledged-finding marker beside it (ADR-013 am. 12 R1). LOAD-BEARING FOR CI: the
# logs above are committed, and check_live_flight_log.py fails HARD on a closest-approach breach
# that has no marker. Without this line CI checks out the breaching logs without their
# acknowledgements and goes red on recorded history it cannot re-fly.
!eval/results/live_flight_log_*.SAFETY_FINDING.md
!eval/results/gate2_summary.json
!eval/results/testflight_gate_*.json
!eval/results/bird_drive_*.json
# ...and the applied-pose log beside it (ADR-003 am. 6): a committed clip's bird labels are DERIVED
# from this file, so without it those labels can never be re-verified — the same lesson as the
# clobbered demo log. Bounded by flight length (~3k lines / ~0.7 MB for a 14-minute mission), never
# frame data. Prune stale runs' logs by hand rather than re-ignoring the class.
!eval/results/bird_drive_*_applied.jsonl
!eval/results/bench_transport_*.json
# The ADR-003 verdict run's scores (am. 7: the ADOPT decision's own evidence — labels,
# detections, spike_scores; overlays excluded below as regenerable imagery)
!eval/results/adr003_*/
# ...with ONE exception, and the word "regenerable" above is why it is needed: overlays regenerate
# only from the clip's FRAMES, and those are never committed (3.8 GB of .npy/.png per flight,
# excluded below). So a fresh checkout can reproduce every number in this directory and not one
# picture. The 2026-08-25 take's four stills (~60 KB) are the only in-repo form of the flagship
# flight's 2-frame encounter — the README and demo figures point at them. Contents-exclude + child
# negation, not a directory exclude: a `dir/` exclude cannot be pierced (see the note above).
# Regenerate with:  python3 eval/label_from_sim.py --clip eval/results/adr003_20260825/clipview \
#   --out <tmp>/gt.json --overlay eval/results/adr003_20260825/overlays --overlay-frames 964 965 \
#   --overlay-detections eval/results/adr003_20260825/detections_ndvi.json
eval/results/adr003_*/overlays/*
!eval/results/adr003_20260825/overlays/*.png
# ADR-003 criterion 2's RGB pixel study (~28 KB of summary metrics, no frames). Committed for the
# same reason as the applied-pose logs: eval/baseline_rgb.py's real-render threshold is DERIVED
# from the class means in this results.json, and tests/fieldguard_planning/test_rgb_pixel_study.py
# recomputes it from here — without the file the constant loses its evidence.
!eval/results/criterion2_rgb_study_*/
!eval/results/clips/
eval/results/clips/*
!eval/results/clips/real_flight_*/
eval/results/clips/real_flight_*/*
!eval/results/clips/real_flight_*/meta.json
!eval/results/clips/real_flight_*/poses.jsonl
!eval/results/clips/real_flight_*/heatmap/
!eval/results/clips/real_flight_*/INVALID_DO_NOT_USE.md

# Generated docs site (the generator is the tracked artifact; the site is disposable —
# rebuild with `python3 scripts/build_docs_site.py`, ADR-014)
docs-site/
